# Cursor Rules for Application Generator

## Project Overview
- **Project**: Application Generator - AI-powered cover letter and CV generator with cognitive training games
- **Main File**: Application_Generator.html (inline CSS + JavaScript)
- **Deployment**: Vercel (https://apply4job.vercel.app)
- **Stack**: Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS, Node.js API (appgen-api/)

## Code Style & Conventions

### HTML/Template Style
- Use semantic HTML5 elements (`<dialog>`, `<nav>`, `<section>`, etc.)
- Modal dialogs: Use native `<dialog>` element with `showModal()` / `close()`
- Data attributes: Use `data-*` for state management (`data-field`, `data-mode`, etc.)
- Class naming: `kebab-case` (e.g., `.toolbar-group`, `.modal-dialog-button`)
- ID naming: `camelCase` (e.g., `#toolbarMoreLetter`, `#applicationForm`)

### CSS Style
- Inline CSS in `<style>` blocks (no separate stylesheet in Application_Generator.html)
- Media queries for responsive design:
  - Mobile: `<640px` (collapsible sections by default)
  - Desktop: `≥640px` (expanded sections by default)
- CSS variables for theming (colors, spacing, typography)
- Flexbox for layouts; grid for complex grids
- Animation: Use `@keyframes` for smooth transitions

### JavaScript Style
- Function naming: `camelCase` (e.g., `toggleToolbarGroup()`, `closeToolbarDialog()`)
- Event handlers: Inline `onclick` or `addEventListener()`
- State management: DOM attributes (`data-*`, classes like `.expanded`)
- Async patterns: Use `async/await` for API calls (not `.then()` chains)
- DOM queries: Use `document.querySelector()` / `document.querySelectorAll()`

### Class Naming Conventions
- `.toolbar-group` - Container for grouped toolbar actions
- `.toolbar-group-label` - Label text inside toolbar group
- `.toolbar-group-primary` - Primary action button
- `.toolbar-group-expand` - Expand/collapse toggle button
- `.toolbar-group-expand-btn` - Specific selector for toggle button
- `.toolbar-group-options` - Container for dropdown/modal options
- `.toolbar-more-dialog` - Modal dialog for toolbar options
- `.toolbar-more-dialog__content` - BEM modifier for dialog content
- `.toolbar-more-dialog-icon` - SVG icon inside dialog button
- `.expanded` - State class indicating expanded/open state (use instead of `.collapsed`)
- `.wtd-game-lab` - Cognitive training mode class
- `.wtd-2d-play` - 2D play area in HUD

## Modal Dialog Patterns

### Structure
```html
<dialog id="toolbarMoreLetter" class="toolbar-more-dialog">
  <div class="toolbar-more-dialog__backdrop"></div>
  <div class="toolbar-more-dialog__content">
    <button class="btn" onclick="editLetter()">
      <svg class="toolbar-more-dialog-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><!-- icon --></svg>
      <span>Edit</span>
    </button>
  </div>
</dialog>
```

### Dialog Functions
- `closeToolbarDialog(dialogId)` - Close any dialog by ID
- `showDialog(dialogId)` - Open dialog (use `dialog.showModal()`)
- Modal backdrop: Semi-transparent overlay that closes dialog on click

### Icons
- SVG icons: Inline in HTML with `<svg class="toolbar-more-dialog-icon">`
- Icon size: 20×20px (flex-shrink: 0)
- Icon gap from text: 10px (flexbox gap)
- Use `currentColor` for dynamic color inheritance

## Mobile Responsiveness

### Breakpoints
- Mobile: `max-width: 639px` - Toolbars collapse to icons only, options hidden
- Desktop: `min-width: 640px` - Toolbars expanded, options visible

### Mobile Toolbar Behavior
- Label text hidden on mobile (show icon only)
- Expand button visible on mobile to toggle options
- Options container hidden by default on mobile (show when `.expanded`)
- Three-dot menu expands upward to avoid viewport cutoff

### Testing Responsive Design
- Use browser DevTools device emulation
- Test at exactly 640px boundary
- Verify chevron rotation and option visibility

## API Integration

### Cloud API Endpoints
- `POST /api/applications` - Save application with `content` field
- `GET /api/applications/:id` - Retrieve application with theme data
- Content field structure:
  ```javascript
  {
    letterThemes: { /* theme config */ },
    openingTemplate: { /* template data */ }
  }
  ```

### Async Patterns
```javascript
async function saveApplication(data) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch('/api/applications', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify(data)
    });
    return await response.json();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Save failed:', error);
  }
}
```

## Cognitive Training (WTD) Integration

### Game Modes
- `wtd-game-lab` - Main cognitive training container
- `.wtd-2d-play` - 2D HUD area for training sessions
- `.wtd-footer` - Black background (#0f172a) in 3D mode

### HUD Functions
- `render2dHud()` - Render training interface header/footer
- `setWtdMode(mode)` - Switch between game modes
- Session start buttons: Center-aligned in HUD area

## Deployment & Build

### Vercel Deployment
- Deploy command: `vercel deploy --target production --yes --scope tokenizin-projects` (from `appgen-api/`)
- Build output: Served from `appgen-api/public/` or static assets
- Environment variables: Configure in Vercel dashboard

### Build Commands
```bash
# From appgen-api/ directory
vercel deploy --target production --yes --scope tokenizin-projects
```

## Git & Version Control

### Commit Messages
- Format: `[feat|fix|refactor|docs|test]: <description>`
- Example: `feat: add icon support to modal dialogs`
- Keep descriptions concise and focused on single feature/fix

### Branch Strategy
- `main` - Production-ready code (deployed to Vercel)
- `dev` - Development branch (preview deployments)
- Feature branches: `feat/feature-name`, `fix/bug-name`

## Testing & Validation

### Manual Testing Checklist
- [ ] Modal dialogs open/close correctly
- [ ] Icons render at 20×20px
- [ ] Toolbar collapses correctly on mobile (<640px)
- [ ] Toolbar expands correctly on desktop (≥640px)
- [ ] Theme persistence: Save and reload application
- [ ] API calls return expected `content` field with theme data
- [ ] Cognitive training HUD renders without errors
- [ ] No console errors in browser DevTools

### Browser Support
- Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)
- Mobile browsers (iOS Safari, Chrome Android)
- CSS Grid, Flexbox, native `<dialog>` support required

## Common Patterns & Do's/Don'ts

### Do
- Use `.expanded` class for state management
- Use native `<dialog>` for modals
- Keep functions focused and single-responsibility
- Add aria-labels to interactive elements
- Test responsive behavior at 640px boundary
- Commit frequently with clear messages

### Don't
- Use `.collapsed` class (use `.expanded` instead)
- Use `display: none` for dialogs (use `<dialog>` or set `display: flex` with visibility)
- Hardcode colors (use CSS variables when possible)
- Forget to close dialogs on overlay click
- Mix inline `onclick` and `addEventListener()` on same element
- Commit without testing on actual Vercel deployment

